1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,180
data minimization.

2
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:04,510
So the idea of data minimization is that you

3
00:00:04,510 --> 00:00:06,820
expose the minimum amount of data required to

4
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:07,840
answer the question being asked.

5
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,120
So if I ask the question,

6
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:10,640
is this person currently free to marry?

7
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:11,870
That's a yes or no answer.

8
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:13,680
Answering that question does not require

9
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,250
showing when they got married,

10
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:16,020
who they married,

11
00:00:16,020 --> 00:00:17,300
when they divorced,

12
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:18,500
which court granted it,

13
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,100
right? Like in the case of Marrify in Ghana,

14
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:21,850
for example,

15
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:22,600
the question is,

16
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:23,760
is this person married?

17
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:24,860
So the answer is simple.

18
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:26,800
This person currently has an active marriage

19
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:27,600
on record.

20
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:28,240
Nothing else.

21
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:29,240
No name of spouse,

22
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:29,820
no dates,

23
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:30,780
no history.

24
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,010
But of course,

25
00:00:32,010 --> 00:00:33,860
another person could request another thing.

26
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:35,800
And then I was thinking about access level.

27
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,940
Maybe perhaps an individual could access a

28
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:39,660
particular level of this data.

29
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:41,320
And maybe there are certain organizations or

30
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:43,467
institutions that can access more.
